```
function rgbToHsv(rgb) {
  // Convert RGB to HSV
  let h = 0;
  let s = 0;
  let v = 0;

  // Calculate Hue
  const r = rgb.r / 255;
  const g = rgb.g / 255;
  const b = rgb.b / 255;
  const max = Math.max(r, g, b);
  const min = Math.min(r, g, b);
  const delta = max - min;
  h = (delta === 0 ? 0 : (max === r ? 60 * (g - b) / delta : 60 * (b - g) / delta));

  // Calculate Saturation
  s = (max === 0 ? 0 : delta / max);

  // Calculate Value
  v = max;

  // Return HSV values
  return { h, s, v };
}
```
This function takes an RGB color object with properties `r`, `g`, and `b` representing the red, green, and blue values, respectively. It then calculates the hue, saturation, and value of the color using the formulas provided in the article you linked.

